          ],
          "text": "You came in after having a seizure at work. It was your first seizure. During the seizure your whole body shook. This is called a generalised tonic-clonic seizure. Afterwards you were confused for a time. You also had a bite on the side of your tongue."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team did several tests:\n- Blood tests, including a check of your blood sugar — these were normal\n- A test to check for substances in your body (toxicology screen) — this was negative\n- A scan of your head (CT scan) — this was normal\n\nThe team did not start any anti-seizure medicine. This is because it was your first seizure."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "The following have been arranged for you:\n- An MRI scan of your brain\n- A brain wave test (EEG)\n- A referral to a first-fit clinic\n\nNeurology will decide about any further treatment after these tests. Your GP has been made aware and will wait to hear the outcome from neurology."
        },
        {
